# Designer workflow (before coding)

Run these checks at the start of every session that implements or changes the prototype.

## 1. Dependencies

- Check that dependencies are installed (`node_modules` present / project can start).
- If missing or the app fails to start because of deps — install with `npm ci` (prefer) or `npm install`.
- Do not reinstall when deps are already present and working.

## 2. Branch

- Check the current git branch before editing.
- Never commit or push work directly on `main`.
- If the designer is on `main` (or another protected/base branch):
  1. Propose a branch name in the format `feature-short-description` (see README).
  2. Agree the name with the designer.
  3. Only then create the branch and switch to it (`git switch -c …`).
- If already on a valid `feature-*` branch, continue there.

## 3. Then proceed

Only after deps and branch are OK: read Figma / implement the mockup / run `npm run dev` and checks from README.
